| Opus V V1R2 reference, qualification, executor, and incident packages | Existing target/build/V5/C10/P3/C0/C3/C8 contracts | Field-level diff only; preserve conflicting lineages; do not apply package patches or select a canonical formula |

### Inventory execution-readiness boundary

Do not collapse availability into one boolean:

- Cypress EO is owned neat/as supplied but not execution-ready until supplier, botanical identity, and lot are bound.
- PADMA / Phenylacetaldehyde Dimethyl Acetal is owned neat and execution-ready.
- Ambrettolide 10% DPG is design-available/planned acquisition only, not execution-ready until physical receipt and ExactStockRef.
- Beta Ionone neat is a current execution-ready stock with active fraction 1.0.
- Beta Ionone 0.1% is a separate working dilution with active fraction 0.001 and is not execution-ready until preparation/carrier lineage closes.
- A nominal Beta Ionone 1% requirement is `PREPARATION_REQUIRED`; the 0.1% stock must never be dosed as if it were 1%.

The live inventory and V5 snapshot already encode these states, so no inventory mutation is justified.

## Installation sequence after user approval

### Gate I0 — Freeze and rollback

1. Recheck branch, HEAD, index tree, staged count, and full status.
2. Create a fresh path-preserving PAX archive immediately before the first repository mutation.
3. Materialize the archive into a short workspace restore root using Windows long-path handling.
4. Hash every restored regular file against the archive manifest.
5. Bind the exact HEAD, index tree, status inventory, archive SHA, manifest SHA, and restore receipt.

No mutation starts if restoration replay is incomplete.

### Gate I1 — Exact package receipts

1. Retain all bytes in quarantine.
2. Reuse an existing canonical package receipt when an exact archive SHA already has one.
3. For a new archive, create one authority-false receipt with exact local locator, size, SHA, root/member counts, embedded ledgers, scanner status, and blockers.
4. Record `promotion=false`, `redistribution=false` unless separately proven, and all scientific/operational authorities false.
5. Never copy an external archive merely to change its locator class.

### Gate I2 — P6 recovery

Recover the original, unchanged bytes only:

- package SHA-256 `8224f8a1609deb22b43651da825b9bf653a92143f00ee1d5d592130d162f97db`
- wheel SHA-256 `582ae9902e47807f085a61b7add113c9239a2860445e8171fcf569b3ad6d28c5`

Require filename, byte size, MIME, outer SHA, safe archive names, CRC, internal ledger replay, nested graph terminality, and source/chat/content-reference lineage. No substitute v1.3 package and no reconstruction from prose.

The exact source chat was prompted after the local/mirror scans. It reported both objects `UNAVAILABLE`, supplied no replacement, and found zero matches across 131 active-runtime files, 21 ZIP-compatible archives, and 1,236 nested members. This confirms the block in that runtime; it does not prove global absence.

### Gate I3 — Field-level native mapping

For every recovered data field, record:

- source path and exact parent hash;
- native destination field or explicit no-fit state;
- transform name/version/config hash;
- `DEPENDS_ON`, `INVARIANT_UNDER`, and invalidation scope;
- authority before and after, which must remain false;
- round-trip preservation test.

Reject fields that attempt to promote package stock labels, float-only active lineage, proxy OAV, template observations, inferred commercial formula truth, or hedonic design scores.

### Gate I4 — Additive implementation only where a gap is proven

Expected default: no migration and no new store.

- Extend native read-only projections or adapters only when I3 proves a real information-loss gap.
- P6, if recovered, receives a source-specific adapter into the native C3/C8 boundary.
- Universal complexity/support-socket records, if recovered, become design candidates linked to target and experiment hashes; they do not create formula rows or empirical observations.
- Chat 2 screens map to C10/P3/C0 planning contracts; physical execution remains separately authorized through Laboratory Beta.

### Gate I5 — Verification

1. Run focused receipt/scanner regressions.
2. Run field-mapping and round-trip tests.
3. Run C10/P3/C0/Laboratory Beta integration tests.
4. Run V5 stock/product-basis negative tests.
5. Run C3/C8 tests only if P6 is implemented.
6. Run the quick project verifier.
7. Run full release verification only if making a release claim.

Required negative cases include unknown stock strength, stale parent hashes, package stock-label promotion, template-row import, missing expected-cell coverage, product-basis active-fraction inference, proxy OAV promotion, and any authority-bit flip.

### Gate I6 — Acceptance receipt

The handoff may say implementation complete only when exact input bytes, local changes, tests, rollback archive, and final artifact hashes are sealed. It still may not claim physical, sensory, safety, formula, inventory, OAV, publication, or release authority unless each separate native gate passes.

